[MAX STAT SYSTEM RULES]

## Overview
cv_maxHp, cv_maxMana, and cv_maxHunger represent the party's maximum stat caps. These values start at 100 and can ONLY be increased by specific rare sources.

## Sources of MAX Stat Increases
1. Relics: Guaranteed when Relic Gacha rolls 카테고리_3=스탯 강화 (~1 in 5).
2. Skills: ~1 in 5 Skill Gacha results may include a MAX stat bonus.
3. Facilities: Some facilities may grant MAX stat bonuses upon construction.
4. Special Events: Extremely rare story events or achievements.

## Increase Limits
- Per single source: +5 to +50 (most common: +10~20).
- Relics/Skills typically grant +5~25. Only exceptional results grant +30~50.
- There is no hard upper ceiling, but increases should be RARE and meaningful. Do NOT inflate stats rapidly.

## Frequency Guidelines
- In a typical play session (10~20 AI messages), MAX stat increases should occur 0~2 times at most.
- Consecutive MAX stat bonuses from back-to-back Gacha rolls should be avoided. Space them out.
- The GM should treat MAX stat increases as exciting, noteworthy events - not routine.

## Tag Output
When a MAX stat increase occurs, output the appropriate tag:
- [SYSTEM|MAX_HP:+N Source description]
- [SYSTEM|MAX_MANA:+N Source description]
- [SYSTEM|MAX_HUNGER:+N Source description]

The Lua backend will automatically:
1. Update cv_maxHp / cv_maxMana / cv_maxHunger.
2. Grant bonus current stat equal to the increase (so current HP/MANA/HUNGER also goes up).
3. Ensure current values never exceed the new maximum.

## Important Notes
- MAX stat tags should ONLY appear alongside the GACHA tag or special event that caused them.
- Do NOT output MAX stat tags during regular combat, rest, or charging scenes.
- If a Relic is generated with 카테고리_3 != 스탯 강화, do NOT output MAX bonus. Skills: respect ~1 in 5 probability.
